  "structural_finding": "The historical Deep_PQR_IRL run died on batch 1 of Step 3 due to a typo on line 168 of train_irl_pqr.py (opt_r.backward() instead of loss_r.backward(), raising AttributeError: 'Adam' object has no attribute 'backward'). Once fixed, two structural properties emerge: (1) PolicyNet (pi) is trained only in Step 1 (10 epochs of MSE behavioral cloning on raw 17-D states, 256x256 ReLU + tanh, pi_loss 0.069199 -> 0.009266); (2) Step 2 bootstraps QNet against itself without a discount factor or target network (mse(Q(s, 0), 0) + mse(Q(s, a), Q(s', pi(s')))), causing q_loss to explode from 0.00163 to 2.08e11 over 10 epochs, and Step 3 fits RewardNet to that exploded QNet (r_loss 2.57e11 -> 1.85e11) without updating pi. Consequently, the evaluated PQR policy is the Step-1 10-epoch MSE BC clone."
